# Default: normalise to LF in the repository, let Git decide in the working tree.
# This must come FIRST -- in gitattributes the LAST matching rule wins, so the overrides
# below would be silently ignored if the wildcard were listed after them.
* text=auto

# Samsung's supplied kit is checksummed BYTE FOR BYTE and must never be translated.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout and a fresh clone fails its own immutability test: data/schema.py becomes 67
# CRLFs instead of 67 LFs and its SHA-256 changes from 649440e0...6ebf6b to
# 833e54d2...069406. The working tree never showed it, because the working tree still
# held the bytes that were committed; only a clean clone does.
#
# -text disables end-of-line conversion in both directions.
data/** -text
backend/app/schema_samsung.py -text

# Generated artefacts: do not try to diff or merge these by hand.
evaluation/report.json -diff
frontend/package-lock.json -diff
